{title: Where You Go, I Will Go}
{subtitle: Ruth 1:8–18}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Go back, my [F/A]daughters, [Gm]each to her [Dm7]mother's house
[Eb]May the Lord deal kind[Gm]ly with [F]you
[Eb]As you have dealt with the [Gm]dead and with [F]me
[Eb]Go back, there is [F7]nothing for you with [Bb]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Do not urge me to [F/A]leave you
[Gm]Or to return from [Dm]following you
[Eb]For where you go, I will [Gm]go
And [F]where you [Eb]lodge, I will [F]lodge
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Your [Bb]people shall be my [F/A]people
And your [Gm]God my [Dm]God
Where you [Eb]die, I will [Bb]die
[Cm]And there I will [F]be buried
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Turn back like your [Gm]sister has turned
[Bb]Back to her people and her [F]gods
[Eb]No, I will not [Gm]leave you
May the [Cm7]Lord do so to me if anything but death parts [F]me from you
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Your people shall be my [F/A]people
And your [Gm]God my [Dm]God
Where you [Eb]die, I will [Bb]die
[Cm]And there I will [F]be buried
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
